{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RBiScWRcgQoh5odWy4RC6v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a thorough understanding of the experiment data and paper framing. Let me synthesize this for the \"worst\" tier paper.\n\nThe key narrative shift for the \"worst\" tier:\n- Core narrative reframed from \"strategy-specific phase interaction\" to \"universal phase vulnerability in compound sparsity\"\n- GPQA data shows random eviction produces comparable phase gradients to importance (ratio <1.5×)\n- Importance gradient shows non-monotonicity at s025→s030\n- Strategy specificity only strong in MATH-500 DeepSeek (15-17×), all other conditions ≤3×\n\n\n- Phase vulnerability emerges as the novel finding, with recency as the only truly robust strategy across conditions, while importance's advantage collapses when discrimination fails\n\nNow I'm structuring the full LaTeX paper to cover all experiments with actual numbers from the data, organized as Abstract through Conclusion, framing these weakened findings honestly as a characterization of universal phase vulnerabilities rather than strategy-specific effects.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14851,"cache_read_input_tokens":24346,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14851},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cbe83670-1763-4df0-a729-5b95d9e54139","uuid":"b213fb97-dd7c-4db3-b051-d9b12a59ec41"}
